.DS_Store
tmp/

# Deployment-specific build/self-test drivers. Kept OUT of this public fork because they carry
# site-specific values (host serials, LAN camera URLs, credentials) that must never enter a public
# git history — once committed, a password stays in the history forever even after deletion.
# The fork's own sources and unit tests stay generic and committed; only these drivers are local.
build_clean.sh
check-syntax.sh
test/scratch_*

# Unit-test build artifacts: `make run` in test/ produces bare executables (no extension) and, on
# macOS, .dSYM debug bundles. Commit the SOURCES only — the binaries are per-arch and multi-MB.
test/test_*
!test/test_*.cpp
test/*.dSYM/

# Library build artifacts. `genMakefiles` writes a Makefile into every subdirectory, and a `make`
# then leaves ~200 .o files plus the static libs — all untracked, all per-arch, none of them source.
# Without these rules `git status` is ~250 lines of noise and a single `git add -A` commits the lot
# (the macOS .dSYM bundles were staged exactly that way once already). Sources are committed; build
# output never is. test/Makefile IS source — it is hand-written, not generated.
*.o
*.a
Makefile
!test/Makefile

# Built executables (per-arch, multi-MB): the proxy under proxyServer/, and the other program
# directories' outputs when a full `make` succeeds.
proxyServer/live555ProxyServer
mediaServer/live555MediaServer
hlsProxy/live555HLSProxy

# Test media
*.264
